# Angels We Have Heard on High, arranged by DeepSeek Flash and SZ. The Gloria refrain on the arp first, then three verses of pulse-wave carol; last verse up a step.
title: Angels We Have Heard on High
composer: Traditional (French)
arranger: DeepSeek Flash & SZ
about: A French carol, Les anges dans nos campagnes. James Chadwick translated it in 1862, keeping the Latin refrain Gloria in excelsis Deo, which imitates the angels' chorus from the Christmas story. Its tune is sometimes called Gloria, and the same melody carries Angels from the Realms of Glory.
year: traditional
source: public-domain
category: carols
key: F major
style: chiptune
tempo: 126
time: 4/4
# balance-ok @1-66 bass: the triangle bass is the chip mix's low end and holds the final cadence; the chip kick is a short noise click with almost no sub

track melody role=lead vol=0.95
